transport ministers meeting today in  Luxembourg discussed how to improve rail  services in the EU through a possible  market opening for domestic passenger  services and stronger governance  according to the Italian presidency it  was a broad and very discussion on the  technical and political pillars of the  fourth whale whale package we discussed  the technical pender the political  pillar the reciprocity clause opening of  domestic passenger markets and the radio  super re lechesa you need to guarantee  equal access to procurement tenders to  the rolling stock we also talked about  cherry-picking namely that we should  guarantee that people don't just  participate in the markets that are  profitable but they should be present  everywhere the council adopted also a  general approach on new rules for access  to the port services market in the EU  and to ensure the financial transparency  of ports the objective of the new rules  is to promote fair competition and  reduce legal uncertainties they also  reached the general approach on a draft  directive to facilitate the cross-border  exchange of information on road traffic  offenses such as speeding not using a  seat belt talking on the phone or  driving under the influence of alcohol  and drugs finally and for the first time  ministers had a look at the  possibilities for the civil use of  drones  you
 

